---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";

// Every figure on this page is copied from the generated reports in the
// repository — docs/measurements-forms.md and docs/measurements-forms-time.md
// — rather than retyped from memory. Where a number here and a number there
// disagree, the report is right and this page is stale.
const counts = [
  ["react-hook-form (scoped)", "0", "0", "0", false],
  ["hand-written per-field state", "1", "209", "5", false],
  ["TanStack Form", "1", "210", "5", false],
  ["form-contract", "1", "212", "5", true],
  ["Formik (FastField)", "2", "1623", "6", false],
  ["Formik (useField)", "2", "2422", "1610", false],
];

const times = [
  ["TanStack Form", "on-change", "4.06x", "5920 µs", "100%", "slower", false],
  ["Formik (useField)", "on-change", "3.87x", "2581 µs", "100%", "slower", false],
  ["Formik (FastField)", "on-change", "2.28x", "2064 µs", "100%", "slower", false],
  ["react-hook-form (scoped)", "on-change", "0.92x", "687 µs", "100%", "indistinguishable", false],
  ["react-hook-form (deps)", "on-change", "0.85x", "1132 µs", "100%", "indistinguishable", false],
  ["form-contract", "on-change", "0.63x", "476 µs", "0%", "indistinguishable", true],
  ["react-hook-form (on-submit)", "on-submit", "0.32x", "323 µs", "0%", "faster", false],
];

const ladder = [
  ["0.1 ms", "not resolved", "not resolved", "not resolved"],
  ["0.25 ms", "not resolved", "not resolved", "not resolved"],
  ["0.5 ms", "resolved", "not resolved", "not resolved"],
  ["1 ms", "resolved", "not resolved", "not resolved"],
  ["2 ms", "resolved", "not resolved", "not resolved"],
  ["4 ms", "resolved", "not resolved", "not resolved"],
];
---

<Base
  title="Benchmark — form-contract"
  description="Two lanes: deterministic counts gated in CI, and microseconds from Chrome's own trace that are printed and never gated. The harness publishes its own resolution above its results."
>
  <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold sm:text-4xl">What the benchmark can, and cannot, see</h1>

  <p class="mt-6 leading-relaxed text-on-surface-variant">
    Five form runtimes plus a hand-written reference are driven through one
    scripted transcript against <strong class="text-on-surface"
      >one zod schema the harness owns and instruments</strong
    >, rendering <strong class="text-on-surface">one DOM the harness owns and
    hashes</strong>. No count is produced by code an adapter author wrote:
    renders come from fiber alternates, validation work from a harness-owned
    schema wrapper, DOM changes from a <code>MutationObserver</code>. There is
    no counter to place favourably.
  </p>

  <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-on-surface-variant">
    Nothing is printed until six proofs hold — that every subject reached the
    same schema instance, judged the same root, rendered the same DOM, is
    actually wired up, and that the oracle would have noticed had it not been.
  </p>

  <!-- ================================================== counts -->
  <h2 class="mt-16 text-2xl font-bold">The counts lane, which is gated</h2>
  <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-on-surface-variant">
    Commits, changed fibers, DOM mutations and validator passes are integers
    that do not depend on the machine, which is the only reason a CI gate can
    exist at all. A drift is therefore never noise.
  </p>

  <p class="mt-8 font-medium">One keystroke that moves no verdict, 201 rendered fields</p>
  <div class="mt-3 overflow-x-auto">
    <table class="w-full text-sm">
      <thead class="text-left text-on-surface-variant">
        <tr class="hairline">
          <th class="py-2 pr-4 font-medium">subject</th>
          <th class="py-2 pr-4 font-medium">commits</th>
          <th class="py-2 pr-4 font-medium">changed fibers</th>
          <th class="py-2 font-medium">host fibers</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {
          counts.map(([name, commits, fibers, host, mine]) => (
            <tr class:list={["hairline", mine && "bg-surface-low"]}>
              <td class:list={["py-2 pr-4", mine && "font-medium"]}>{name}</td>
              <td class="py-2 pr-4">{commits}</td>
              <td class="py-2 pr-4">{fibers}</td>
              <td class="py-2">{host}</td>
            </tr>
          ))
        }
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <p class="mt-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-on-surface-variant">
    form-contract is fourth on this table and the report sorts the rows it loses
    first. The scoped react-hook-form configuration commits nothing for a
    keystroke that does not move a verdict — and the same row records that it
    still ran a full schema pass to find that out, which is why{" "}
    <code>validatorPasses</code> sits on every row beside the render counts: a
    zero-commit row can never be read as free.
  </p>

  <!-- ================================================== resolution -->
  <h2 class="mt-16 text-2xl font-bold">
    The timing lane publishes its resolution <em>before</em> its results
  </h2>
  <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-on-surface-variant">
    A known cost is injected at seven sizes and three scheduling positions, and
    each subject is run against a byte-identical twin of itself at every size.
    A band that overlaps the twin's band prints{" "}
    <code>indistinguishable</code>, never a win.
  </p>

  <div class="mt-6 overflow-x-auto">
    <table class="w-full text-sm">
      <thead class="text-left text-on-surface-variant">
        <tr class="hairline">
          <th class="py-2 pr-4 font-medium">injected</th>
          <th class="py-2 pr-4 font-medium">synchronous</th>
          <th class="py-2 pr-4 font-medium">microtask</th>
          <th class="py-2 font-medium">macrotask</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {
          ladder.map(([size, sync, micro, macro]) => (
            <tr class="hairline">
              <td class="py-2 pr-4 font-mono text-xs">{size}</td>
              <td class:list={["py-2 pr-4", sync === "resolved" && "font-medium"]}>
                {sync}
              </td>
              <td class="py-2 pr-4">{micro}</td>
              <td class="py-2">{macro}</td>
            </tr>
          ))
        }
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <p class="mt-5 rounded-lg bg-surface-container p-5 leading-relaxed">
    <strong>This harness sees 0.5 ms of synchronous work, and nothing at all up
    to 4 ms of work deferred to a microtask.</strong> The headline metric is the{" "}
    <code>EventDispatch</code> trace event filtered to <code>input</code>, and
    that event closes before a microtask runs. A runtime that defers its work —
    form-contract coalesces its validation pass to a microtask — is therefore
    cheap on this metric <em>by construction</em>.
  </p>

  <!-- ================================================== times -->
  <h2 class="mt-16 text-2xl font-bold">The timing lane, which is never gated</h2>
  <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-on-surface-variant">
    Headless Chrome, 21 interleaved pairs per comparison, both members of a pair
    inside one tracing session on two origins. Ratios are against the
    hand-written per-field reference at 201 fields; above 1 means slower.
    Timings move when the runner does, so this lane prints and CI never fails on
    it.
  </p>

  <div class="mt-6 overflow-x-auto">
    <table class="w-full text-sm">
      <thead class="text-left text-on-surface-variant">
        <tr class="hairline">
          <th class="py-2 pr-4 font-medium">subject</th>
          <th class="py-2 pr-4 font-medium">policy</th>
          <th class="py-2 pr-4 font-medium">ratio</th>
          <th class="py-2 pr-4 font-medium">handler</th>
          <th class="py-2 pr-4 font-medium">pass inside it</th>
          <th class="py-2 font-medium">verdict</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {
          times.map(([name, policy, ratio, handler, inside, verdict, mine]) => (
            <tr class:list={["hairline", mine && "bg-surface-low"]}>
              <td class:list={["py-2 pr-4", mine && "font-medium"]}>{name}</td>
              <td class="py-2 pr-4 text-on-surface-variant">{policy}</td>
              <td class="py-2 pr-4">{ratio}</td>
              <td class="py-2 pr-4">{handler}</td>
              <td class="py-2 pr-4">{inside}</td>
              <td class="py-2">{verdict}</td>
            </tr>
          ))
        }
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <p class="mt-5 rounded-lg bg-surface-container p-5 leading-relaxed">
    <strong>The row to read carefully is ours.</strong> form-contract measures
    0.63x the reference and the verdict still says{" "}
    <code>indistinguishable</code>: the 308 µs difference is under the 500 µs
    floor the ladder above established, and the harness separately{" "}
    <em>measures</em> — it does not assume — that 0% of form-contract's
    validation passes ran inside the event being timed. That work is real and it
    is not in the handler figure. The counts lane is where it is counted rather
    than timed.
  </p>

  <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-on-surface-variant">
    The <code>on-submit</code> row is the same caution in the other direction:
    it is genuinely faster per keystroke because, by documented design, it does
    no validation during one at all. Policy is an axis of the matrix rather than
    a defect of the competitor.
  </p>

  <!-- ================================================== excluded -->
  <h2 class="mt-16 text-2xl font-bold">What was measured and then thrown away</h2>
  <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-on-surface-variant">
    Each excluded metric is published with the measurement that excluded it, so
    a reader can check whether the discarded ones happen to be the flattering
    ones. <code>ScriptDuration</code> showed a 245% spread between two
    byte-identical pages. <code>TaskDuration</code> is dominated by the driver's
    own CDP round trip. <code>PerformanceEventTiming.duration</code> is
    quantised to 8 ms, larger than everything published here.
    React's <code>Profiler.actualDuration</code> excludes commit and fires zero
    times in the production build this lane requires. And every millisecond
    taken in jsdom, because jsdom has no layout, no style resolution and no
    paint — on this page layout alone is routinely larger than the script that
    precedes it.
  </p>

  <p class="mt-8 text-sm leading-relaxed text-on-surface-variant">
    Both reports are generated by <code>npm run bench:forms</code> and{" "}
    <code>npm run bench:forms:time</code>, and the design that argues for every
    choice above is in <code>docs/design/form-benchmark.md</code>.
  </p>
</Base>
